    "media_with_text_RGVTzq": {
      "type": "media-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_HRqWaf": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Before Expressing or Handling Breast Milk",
            "heading_size": "h3",
            "heading_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_djDRF9": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Before expressing or handling breast milk, it’s essential to follow proper hygiene and safety guidelines to ensure the quality and safety of the milk. Here are some steps to take:</p><ul><li><strong>Wash Your Hands</strong>: Always wash your hands thoroughly with soap and water before expressing or handling breast milk. Clean hands help prevent the introduction of bacteria and other contaminants into the milk</li><li><strong>Sanitize Equipment</strong>: Ensure your breast pump and storage containers are clean and sanitized before use. This includes all parts that come into contact with the milk.</li><li><strong>Use Clean Devices</strong>: Use a clean and sterile breast pump or expression device to express milk. This helps maintain the purity of the milk.</li><li><strong>Proper Storage</strong>: Store expressed milk in a clean and airtight container, labeling it with the date and time of expression. This helps you keep track of the milk’s freshness.</li><li><strong>Temperature Control</strong>: Store milk in the refrigerator at a temperature of 39°F (4°C) or below, or freeze it at 0°F (-18°C) or below for longer storage. Proper temperature control is crucial for preserving the milk’s quality.</li></ul><p>By following these steps, you can ensure that your expressed milk remains safe and nutritious for your baby.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_HRqWaf",
        "text_djDRF9"
      ],
      "custom_css": [
        ".media {border-radius: 1rem;}",
        ".section--padded {padding-top: 0 !important;}"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/CS_7.png",
