    "media_with_text_MBXhpQ": {
      "type": "media-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_nNWBya": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Choosing the Right Container for Milk Storage",
            "heading_size": "h3",
            "heading_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_JmCMib": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Selecting the right container for breast milk storage is essential to ensure its safety and freshness. Follow these guidelines for effective storage:</p><ul><li><strong>Use Appropriate Containers</strong>: Choose breast milk storage bags or clean, food-grade plastic bottles with tight-fitting lids. These are specifically designed for safe milk storage.</li><li><strong>Avoid Inappropriate Bags</strong>: Avoid disposable bottle liners or plastic bags not intended for breast milk storage, as they can leak or break.</li><li><strong>BPA-Free</strong>: Opt for BPA-free containers, like those from Ameda, to minimize exposure to potentially harmful chemicals.</li><li><strong>Secure Closure</strong>: Ensure your containers have a secure closure to prevent leaks, especially when freezing milk.</li><li><strong>Measurement Markings</strong>: Use containers with clear measurement markings for accurate portioning.</li><li><strong>Check Condition: </strong>Regularly check containers for damage or expiration dates to ensure they remain safe for use.</li></ul><p>By choosing the right storage solutions, you can protect your breast milk and support your breastfeeding journey.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_nNWBya",
        "text_JmCMib"
      ],
      "custom_css": [
